  "reveal": {
    "ledger_voiced": "From my book. The sitting ran as I ran it: the glass, and my hand upon it, as ever. The glass spelled MY CHAIR; the glass goes where I send it.\n\nAs to the evening's business: the account the Colonel swore to was an invention, for those hands were out of the dark and about their own work. Fifi Swain was past any sitting's reach before the lamps were lit.\n\nThe dead say what it profits me they say; on this occasion they profited the Colonel more.",
